{"title":"Career roadmap — Research Assistant (Botany)","role":"Research Assistant (Botany)","summary":"A Botany Research Assistant supports research in plant biology, ecology, taxonomy, plant physiology, genetics, biotechnology, conservation, agriculture, and environmental sciences. Typical work includes sample collection, laboratory experiments, microscopy, plant identification, data analysis, literature review, field studies, documentation, and research publication support.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Botany"},"about":[{"label":"Direct alignment","text":"★★★★★ — B.Sc. Botany provides a strong foundation for entry-level biological research, but M.Sc. specialization is usually important for long-term research careers."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build plant biology, laboratory, fieldwork and research-method skills"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Research Assistant → Project Associate / Junior Research Fellow"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Research Scientist / PhD Researcher / Scientific Officer"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead research projects, laboratories, conservation programmes or applied plant-science teams"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Core learning","Practical exposure"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Plant diversity, cell biology, morphology, anatomy, basic chemistry"},{"text":"Herbarium, microscopy and plant-identification exercises"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Plant physiology, taxonomy, genetics, ecology, microbiology"},{"text":"Field surveys, specimen collection and laboratory experiments"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Molecular biology, biotechnology, conservation, research methodology, statistics"},{"text":"Research internship + independent mini-p